id: decisions/047-unknown-stays-unknown
title: "A missing value is written as missing"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'completeness-versus-honesty'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: completeness-versus-honesty
axis_gloss: "whether every slot is filled so the record looks finished, or slots are left visibly unfilled to stay truthful"
poles:
  a: honest-partial-record
  b: complete-looking-record
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 3.8
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(8) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  When a record does not know a value, must the slot say so (empty,
  not-recorded, a typed lacuna), or may it carry a plausible value so the record
  reads complete?

why_it_matters: >
  Two authored rules say do not invent missing answers and one real receipt
  writes provider_cost: unknown under status proved, but one example carries
  bot_state: sleeping and lifecycle_state: active at once with no transition
  between them. Once answered, a bot writing a receipt knows it must name what
  it failed to capture, and a child Yawn learns that an empty slot is a
  legitimate object it can address rather than a gap to paper over.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    7 judgments sit at honest-partial-record (3 authored) and 1 at
    complete-looking-record (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions
    on this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave counts a self-labelled placeholder such as sha256:example-before
    as honest or as an invented value.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: A value the record does not have is written as an explicit marker (an
      empty string, not-recorded, unknown, or a typed lacuna with a kind). No field
      is filled by inference or synthesis to make the record read complete, and two
      fields that describe the same state may not disagree without a transition
      receipt between them.
    cost: "Fix examples/dave-good-dad-objective-holon.yawn to one lifecycle value or add an activation receipt; name not-recorded/unknown in templates/proof-receipt.yawn."
    risk: "Records fill with unknown markers that satisfy the rule and defer the work."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend scripts/validate-objective-holon-v0.1.mjs to reject an objective holon whose proposed bot_state and realized lifecycle_state disagree with no activation receipt; add not-recorded and unknown to templates/proof-receipt.yawn as the named values for uncaptured fields."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0111"
      - "J0403"
      - "J0407"
      - "J0484"
      - "J0500"
      - "J0640"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: Records may carry placeholder or inferred values so that examples and
      receipts read complete; a reader is expected to know which values are
      illustrative.
    cost: "Withdraws the 'Do not invent missing answers' rule from question-packets/ and the typed-lacuna rule from interface/new-yawn-v0.1.yawn."
    risk: "An invented value enters the record with no attributable source, which is exactly the harm J0500 names."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None can enforce this."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0393"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: As A, except that example fixtures may carry a self-evidently fake
      placeholder (such as sha256:example-before) when the file is marked as an
      example and the placeholder cannot be mistaken for a real value.
    cost: "One marker convention for examples; otherwise as A."
    risk: "The line between an obvious placeholder and a plausible fake is argued per file."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "As A, plus a check that any digest in examples/ either matches the real pattern or contains the word example."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0484"
      - "J0500"
      - "J0640"
      - "J0407"

recommendation:
  option_ref: A
  confidence: 0.8
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    The honest-partial side is authored twice (J0484, J0500), outcome-attached
    once (J0640, a real receipt writing provider_cost: unknown under status
    proved), and revealed three more times. The lone exception, J0393, is not a
    chosen pole but an internal contradiction in one example file: two lifecycle
    fields that disagree with no transition, in a folder whose other examples
    insist activation requires a receipt. It should be fixed, not written down. C
    is not needed: waiting-turn's sha256:example-before already announces itself
    as an example and participation-choice's empty strings are already honest, so
    both satisfy A as stated.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "examples/dave-good-dad-objective-holon.yawn carries one lifecycle value or an activation receipt between bot_state and lifecycle_state."
    - "scripts/validate-objective-holon-v0.1.mjs rejects the disagreement and passes on the fixed file."
    - "templates/proof-receipt.yawn names not-recorded and unknown as the values for fields a run failed to capture."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A receipt with status proved omits provider_cost entirely and no reader can
    tell it was uncaptured rather than free.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J0111"
  - "J0403"
  - "J0407"
  - "J0484"
  - "J0500"
  - "J0640"
  - "J0393"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
